          "Strings are written double-quoted with Zig's escapes, never as multiline string literals.",
          "A character literal and an enum literal are written as the value the reader resolved them to, so neither reads back as a literal.",
          "An empty struct is written .{}, which ZON reads as an empty tuple, so an empty object reads back as an empty array.",
          "An object whose first member is $big, the reader's form of an integer no double holds exactly, is written as the integer its digits spell, and may hold no other member.",
          "ZON has no field name for the empty string, so an object with that key is refused.",
          "A field name holding U+0000 is written with an escape ZON does not read in an identifier, since the render cannot test a name for it."
